                        </Array>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="legend" value="LEGEND PK primary key · FK foreign key · UK unique · PK FK part of a composite primary key  SUBTYPES  department declares UNIQUE (department_id, type). warehouse and branch each pin their own type with a CHECK and reference that composite key, so a department is exactly one of the two — enforced structurally, without a trigger.  ORDERS  branch_id is the sales location where the order was taken; warehouse_id is the warehouse whose stock fills it. order_item.unit_price records the price at the time of sale, so an invoice total is fixed once the order exists.  MANAGERS  department.manager_id is nullable: a department is created before anyone is hired into it. A constraint trigger refuses an outsider as manager, but a sitting manager who transfers or leaves simply vacates the post — losing a manager is normal, having one who works elsewhere is not. v_department_without_manager reports the vacancy for an admin to fill.  LOW STOCK  the reorder point is per part, in part.reorder_level, not a fixed constant; a part left at the default 0 never reports as low.  LOGINS  app_user.employee_id is nullable and unique: a login may belong to no person (a service account), and no person may hold two logins. There is no MANAGER role — v_user_identity derives is_manager from department.manager_id, so promotion stays a single UPDATE.  DERIVED VALUES are views, not columns: v_department_headcount, v_department_without_manager, v_order_total, v_low_stock, and v_user_identity." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="900" width="720" height="310" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>